  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhancing Pacific Engagement - Pacific Law and Justice Program</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Attorney-General&apos;s Department&apos;s (AGD) contribution to the Pacific Law and Justice Program aims to modernise Pacific island countries&apos; policing, law enforcement and criminal justice legislation and policies. This enables law and justice, policing and prosecution agencies to respond more effectively to law and justice issues, including violence against women, corruption, and transnational crime. AGD works with Pacific island countries and the Australian Federal Police and the Department of Foreign Affairs and Trade to develop and implement key components of an improved criminal justice system, both bilaterally and regionally. The Non-ODA component supports the undertaking of projects, including capacity development, that may not meet the ODA eligible guidelines.</narrative>
  </description>
